n, Upper\nYampa River Basin, San Juan River Basin, and Central Colorado River\nBasin.\n\n* WHEN...For the first Freeze Warning, from midnight tonight to 10 AM\nMDT Friday. For the second Freeze Warning, from midnight Friday\nNight to 10 AM MDT Saturday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Frost and freeze conditions could kill crops, other\nsensitive vegetation and possibly damage unprotected outdoor\nplumbing.","ends":"2026-10-17T10:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Lower Yampa River Basin; Central Yampa River Basin; Upper Yampa River Basin; Central Colorado River Basin; San Juan River Basin","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.4921cf80792b8ed73a30525802f9857a9224eb4c.001.3","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.4921cf80792b8ed73a30525802f9857a9224eb4c.001.3"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-10-15T17:40:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 151740 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 1140 AM MDT Thu Oct 15 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - First freeze of the season expected over most of the plains tonight. - Chilly but dry/sunny weather Friday, with another freeze north and east of the Denver metro area Friday night. - Mainly dry and warmer for the weekend through the middle of next week. ","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-10-15T17:07:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Rest of today through Tuesday... Below normal temperatures will continue through Friday night. Much drier air will overspread the forecast area so despite the cooler temperatures humidity values will mostly drop into the 15-22 percent range on Friday but winds will be mostly light. Warmer and drier conditions are expected for the weekend. We could see some locally critical fire weath","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"hyd01","station_name":"Hayden","distance_km":6.8,"soi